---
import SectionWrapper from '../ui/SectionWrapper.astro';
import '../../styles/components/our-work-volume.css';
---
<SectionWrapper background="atmosphere" class="our-work-section our-work-volume-section">
<section id="recognition" class="container container-wide our-work-volume" aria-labelledby="recognition-volume-title">
<header class="our-work-volume-heading">
<div><p class="eyebrow">THE COLLECTION · VOL. 05</p><h2 id="recognition-volume-title">Recognition &amp; Features</h2></div>
<p>A considered record of published materials, event features, and formal recognition connected to the work. Each item is presented as evidence in its own right—not as a substitute for outcomes or impact.</p>
</header>
<div class="work-volume" data-work-volume="recognition">
<div class="work-volume-cover" data-volume-cover>
<div class="work-volume-cover-art" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/media/dfdi-2025.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span class="work-volume-cover-wash"></span><span class="work-volume-cover-index">05</span><span class="work-volume-cover-rule"></span><span class="work-volume-cover-mark">E / D</span></div>
<div class="work-volume-cover-copy"><p class="work-volume-kicker">E DEVISER · SELECTED RECORD</p><h3>A record beyond our own channels.</h3><p class="work-volume-cover-description">Published materials and recognition connected to the conversations, initiatives, and work documented in this collection.</p><div class="work-volume-cover-meta"><span>VOLUME 05</span><span>RECOGNITION &amp; FEATURES</span></div><button class="work-volume-open" type="button" data-volume-open aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="recognition-book-content"><span>Open volume</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><span class="work-volume-spine" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</div>
<div class="work-volume-content" id="recognition-book-content" data-volume-content hidden>
<div class="work-volume-toolbar"><div class="work-volume-location"><span class="work-volume-kicker">THE COLLECTION / 05</span><span data-volume-counter aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">01 / 03</span></div><button class="work-volume-close" type="button" data-volume-close><span>Close volume</span><span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button></div>
<div class="work-volume-pages">
<article class="work-volume-spread is-active" data-volume-page="0" aria-hidden="false"><div class="work-volume-page-copy"><p class="work-volume-page-label">01 / PUBLISHED MATERIAL</p><h3>Documenting the wider conversation.</h3><p>This DFDI 2025 material is included as a published record connected to the work. It gives visitors a source to inspect rather than asking them to rely on a summary written here.</p><span class="work-volume-page-foot">RECOGNITION &amp; FEATURES · DFDI 2025</span></div><figure class="work-volume-page-media work-volume-document-media"><img src="/media/dfdi-2025.webp" alt="DFDI 2025 published material" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption><span>05.01</span> DFDI 2025 · Published material</figcaption></figure></article>
<article class="work-volume-spread" data-volume-page="1" aria-hidden="true" hidden><div class="work-volume-page-copy"><p class="work-volume-page-label">02 / EVENT FEATURE</p><h3>A place in the event record.</h3><p>The Patriot Summit Series material records E Deviser’s connection to the event series. It is presented as an event feature, without extending that record into claims beyond what the material itself establishes.</p><span class="work-volume-page-foot">RECOGNITION &amp; FEATURES · THE PATRIOT</span></div><figure class="work-volume-page-media work-volume-document-media"><img src="/media/the-patriot-summit-series.webp" alt="The Patriot Summit Series event feature" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption><span>05.02</span> The Patriot Summit Series · Event feature</figcaption></figure></article>
<article class="work-volume-spread" data-volume-page="2" aria-hidden="true" hidden><div class="work-volume-page-copy"><p class="work-volume-page-label">03 / CERTIFICATE</p><h3>Recognition, kept in context.</h3><p>This certificate is retained as a documentary item from the EdTech Forum. Its inclusion records the recognition represented by the document, without implying a broader ranking or endorsement.</p><span class="work-volume-page-foot">RECOGNITION &amp; FEATURES · EDTECH FORUM</span></div><figure class="work-volume-page-media work-volume-document-media"><img src="/media/edtech-forum-certificate.webp" alt="EdTech Forum certificate" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption><span>05.03</span> EdTech Forum · Certificate</figcaption></figure></article>
</div>
<div class="work-volume-navigation"><button type="button" data-volume-prev disabled aria-label="Previous spread"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span><span>Previous</span></button><div class="work-volume-progress" role="group" aria-label="Choose a spread"><button type="button" data-volume-go="0" class="is-active" aria-label="Go to spread 1" aria-current="step"></button><button type="button" data-volume-go="1" aria-label="Go to spread 2"></button><button type="button" data-volume-go="2" aria-label="Go to spread 3"></button></div><button type="button" data-volume-next><span>Next</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div>
</div>
</section>
</SectionWrapper>
